WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.304
The provider’s own layer: refusals.

2
00:00:02.584 --> 00:00:07.277
Current Claude models include safety classifiers that can decline a request.

3
00:00:07.557 --> 00:00:19.163
When that happens you get a normal HTTP 200 response with stop_reason set to "refusal" and a stop_details object naming a policy category (which can be null).

4
00:00:19.443 --> 00:00:23.304
A refusal can arrive before any output or partway through a stream.

5
00:00:23.584 --> 00:00:38.368
Anthropic’s docs are specific about what to do: treat any partial output as incomplete and discard it, and reset or rephrase the refused turn before continuing, because continuing the same context tends to produce more refusals.

6
00:00:38.648 --> 00:00:47.608
You can also opt into server-side fallback (in beta), which retries a declined request on a recommended fallback model inside the same call.

7
00:00:47.888 --> 00:00:49.701
Two engineering consequences.

8
00:00:49.981 --> 00:00:55.315
First, a refusal is not an error, so dashboards built only on error rates won’t show it.

9
00:00:55.595 --> 00:01:02.955
Track refusal rate per route as its own signal; a jump usually means a prompt change, a new kind of traffic, or abuse.

10
00:01:03.235 --> 00:01:05.901
Second, refusals include false positives.

11
00:01:06.181 --> 00:01:18.107
Anthropic’s category descriptions say benign work in areas such as cybersecurity can trigger them, which is a reason to show a helpful fixed message and offer a human path rather than a dead end.

12
00:01:18.387 --> 00:01:21.459
It’s worth seeing what provider-side guards cost at scale.

13
00:01:21.739 --> 00:01:37.867
Anthropic reported that its updated Constitutional Classifiers (input and output classifiers trained on synthetic data generated from a written constitution) cut jailbreak success in an automated evaluation from 86 percent to 4.

14
00:01:38.147 --> 00:01:41.539
4 percent, with an increase in over-refusals of 0.

15
00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:47.515
38 percent that wasn’t statistically significant, and about 24 percent more compute.

16
00:01:47.795 --> 00:01:52.104
Even the best-resourced guard has a measured price and a nonzero miss rate.
